### 3. Broken Wiring & Fragile Patterns

1. **Incomplete Public `initKoin()` in [`Koin.kt:72-75`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/di/Koin.kt#L72-L75)**:
   ```kotlin
   fun initKoin() =
       startKoin {
           modules(sharedModule)
       }
   ```
   This function registers only `sharedModule` and omits `appModule`. If any platform caller invokes `initKoin()`, resolving [`PayslipViewModel`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/composeApp/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/ui/PayslipViewModel.kt) fails with `NoBeanDefFoundException`. Fortunately, iOS [`MainViewController.kt:32-36`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/composeApp/src/iosMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/MainViewController.kt#L32-L36) defines its own internal `ensureKoin()` passing `modules(sharedModule, appModule)`. `initKoin()` is dead, misleading, and incomplete.

2. **Static Callback Overwrite in [`IosGemmaBaseModelInstaller.kt:22-37`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/shared/src/iosMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/insights/gemma/GemmaBaseModelInstaller.ios.kt#L22-L37)**:
   `progressReporter` and `completionReporter` are stored as `var`s on the `companion object`. In [`IosGemmaBaseModelInstaller.init`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/shared/src/iosMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/insights/gemma/GemmaBaseModelInstaller.ios.kt#L22), the instance assigns closures capturing its own `_state`. Since [`PayslipViewModel`](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PayslipMAX%20KMP/composeApp/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/ui/PayslipViewModel.kt) is configured in Koin as a `factory` (creating a new instance whenever resolved), resolving a second ViewModel instance overwrites the global static listeners.

