### Remediation Status — Phase 1 (2026-09-21)

**Resolved**
- **Developer Sandbox gate** — `DeveloperSandboxSection` now requires debug or TestFlight via `shouldShowDeveloperSandbox` (covered by `DeveloperSandboxGateTest`).
- **`x86_64` iOS Simulator** — `EXCLUDED_ARCHS[sdk=iphonesimulator*] = x86_64` added to both target build configs. `xcodebuild … generic/platform=iOS Simulator` failed at the x86_64 link before the change and succeeds after. Gradle `iosX64()` targets are intentionally unchanged (they do not use the Xcode link).
- **Dead code removed** — Koin `HttpClient` singleton, `initKoin()` (deleted rather than fixed; iOS uses `ensureKoin()`), `NetworkErrorMapper` (+ test), `UploadWidget` (+ test) and its three orphaned `AppStrings` constants.

**Resolved after the initial Phase 1 commit**
- **Orphaned Ktor build dependencies** removed from `shared/build.gradle.kts` and `composeApp/build.gradle.kts`, plus the `ktor*` entries in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`. No `io.ktor` import remained in any module. Full gate re-run green (check incl. corpus, iOS sim tests, iOS link, `assembleRelease`/R8); release APK ~108 KB smaller. `-dontwarn io.ktor.**` in `composeApp/proguard-rules.pro` is intentionally kept (harmless; guards against transitive references).

**Resolved in the 3.1 phase (2026-09-21)**
- **Firebase anonymous auth and token bridge** removed (Kotlin `auth/` in all source sets, Swift sign-in and `AuthTokenFetcher`, `firebase-auth-ktx`, `FirebaseAuth` Xcode product refs, stale `SignInHubActivity` manifest removal). It had zero production callers; only iOS signed in, on every launch. Full automated gate green; see `08_01_TechDebt_Explanation` §3.1.

**Resolved in the 2.2 phase (2026-09-21)**
- **Room destructive-migration fallback** removed from both platform builders; an unmigratable or unknown DB version now fails loudly instead of wiping payslips. Covered by `PayslipDatabaseUpgradeTest` (unknown version fails and keeps its data; every exported schema version upgrades to head; a payslip survives 5→11). See `08_01_TechDebt_Explanation` §2.2.

**Resolved in the 1.2 phase (2026-09-21)**
- **Static callbacks in the iOS Gemma installer:** the installer is now a Koin `single` in `appModule` (it was never injected, only a default argument, so every ViewModel built its own), and `IosGemmaBaseModelInstaller.install()` collapses overlapping triggers with a `fetchInFlight` flag so the Swift bridge no longer replaces its `NSBundleResourceRequest` mid-download. The companion slots and `GemmaOnDemandResourceBridge.swift` are unchanged. Covered by `GemmaInstallerDiWiringTest` and two new `IosGemmaBaseModelInstallerTest` cases. Full automated gate green; the real-device ODR check is still pending on the next TestFlight build. See `08_01_TechDebt_Explanation` §1.2.

**Consequence to remember**
- The Android **release-build** Crashlytics/R8 symbolication check (used at `docs/Launch/06` v8 and `docs/Plan/06` Phase 11) reached the crash triggers through the Developer Sandbox 7-tap unlock. That path no longer exists in release builds. Future R8 checks must use a debug build or a temporary local build that patches the gate.
